# NOTE: `_headers` applies to STATIC ASSETS ONLY. Responses generated by the
# Worker (any route with `prerender = false`) do not get these headers and will
# need them set in middleware. There are no such routes today.
#
# Keep every `/*` header in this one block. With two `/*` blocks, the local
# server only applies the second.
#
# X-Robots-Tag keeps this deployment out of search results for the duration
# of the rebuild.
#
# The rest are security headers. The site is static, with no cookies, forms
# or third-party scripts, so these only stop other sites from framing it,
# stop type sniffing and turn off browser features it never uses. A full CSP
# would also need hashes for the inlined CSS and scripts. HSTS gets turned on
# in Cloudflare's SSL/TLS settings at the DNS cutover. workers.dev is already
# HTTPS-only.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
